            <ArticleTitle>Intercourse-related vaginal pain syndrome: a variant of &quot;vulvar vestibulitis syndrome&quot;?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>194-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of severe vaginal pain associated with vaginal intercourse and thought to be caused by levator vaginae muscle myalgia is discussed. Both the patient's grandmother and great-grandmother had had identical symptoms; in both of those cases the pain disappeared following the first vaginal delivery of a child.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
